            <div xml:id="d593">

                <pb facs="0562" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/14827: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-16T16:00:00-05:00">December 16,
                            1941—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>303. For the Ambassador from the President. In view of the disruption of mail
                    service, I am acknowledging by telegraph the receipt of your letter of November
                    19 in which you presented an estimate of the situation in China. I found your
                    letter of interest and of value, and I want you to know that during these
                    critical days when the United States and China are fighting side by side against
                    common enemies you and the gallant Government to which you are accredited are
                    very much in my thoughts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
